# Maximum Marginal Likelihood and REML

## Linear Mixed Model

$$
\boldsymbol{y} = \boldsymbol{X} \boldsymbol{\beta} + \boldsymbol{Z} \boldsymbol{b} + \boldsymbol{\epsilon}
$$

:::{.incremental}
- $\boldsymbol{\beta}$ is fixed (the population average)
- $\boldsymbol{b}$ and $\boldsymbol{\epsilon}$ are random (properties of the *sample*)
- all we do is conditional on $\boldsymbol{X}$
- $\boldsymbol{y}$ just follows given the things above
:::

## Need Some Kind of Nesting

$$
y_{ij} = \boldsymbol{x}_{ij}^{T} \boldsymbol{\beta} + \boldsymbol{z}_{ij}^{T} \boldsymbol{b}_{i} + \epsilon_{ij}
$$


